Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 09:45:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 119/154] fix(devbar): let a click in the plate's corner wedges
 reach the page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bar's WebContents sat in a rectangular NSView while the plate is a
17px stadium, and nothing on that path overrides hitTest, so the four
corner wedges swallowed clicks. An AtriumRoundedHitTestView now hosts
the page's NSView and declines a hit outside the rounded rect, swapped
in through WebView's holder once the widget exists. A DevBarWebView
subclass keeps WebView's own re-attach from putting the raw view back,
and the window detaches the wrapper through the holder on teardown.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index b44c41579f291..1cfac057a4229 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3647,6 +3647,8 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_sidebar_edge_reveal.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_overlay_shadow_layer.h",
       "atrium/atrium_overlay_shadow_layer.mm",
+      "atrium/atrium_rounded_hit_test_view.h",
+      "atrium/atrium_rounded_hit_test_view.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_frost_probe.h",
       "atrium/atrium_frost_probe.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_sidebar_frost_layer.h",
